From 992e62dd1f1c4e1c9af882dc8670e3eacc39aeaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 75/76] vulkan/wsi: Horizon, the image count is the mode's when
 the query names one
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 6 item 5 (present modes and scaling)
Why: nvk_instance.c advertises VK_KHR_surface_maintenance1 and
 VK_EXT_surface_maintenance1, so an application may chain
 VkSurfacePresentModeKHR into
 vkGetPhysicalDeviceSurfaceCapabilities2KHR and ask what ONE present
 mode needs. The Vulkan specification says of that query that
 VkSurfaceCapabilitiesKHR::minImageCount and maxImageCount "are valid
 only for the specified presentMode"
 (Vulkan-Docs, chapters/VK_KHR_surface/wsi.adoc). This backend answered
 the BufferQueue's mode-agnostic floor to every such question, while
 wsi_horizon_surface_create_swapchain raised the count to three for
 IMMEDIATE — the compositor honours swapInterval 0 only with three
 buffers registered. So an application that asked what IMMEDIATE costs
 was told two and then given three.
Evidence: measured on a console 2026-09-07,
 sdmc:/horizon_gpu_tests/vk_wsi.log, with this patch applied.
 vk_wsi/swapchain section I asks the surface about one present mode at a
 time and then creates a swapchain at the count it was told:
     I: FIFO wants 2 to 4 images; scaling 0x00000000, gravity
        0x00000000/0x00000000, scaled 16x16 to 1280x720
     I: IMMEDIATE wants 3 to 4 images; scaling 0x00000000, gravity
        0x00000000/0x00000000, scaled 16x16 to 1280x720
     I: FIFO asked for the 2 images its mode advertises and got 2
     I: IMMEDIATE asked for the 3 images its mode advertises and got 3
 Without it both queries answer "2 to 4" and the IMMEDIATE swapchain
 comes back holding three. vk_wsi is PASS 622/622 [3/3] with it.
Upstream: no — the three-buffer floor is the Horizon compositor's rule
 about swapInterval 0, and NWindow exists nowhere else.

ONE FUNCTION, BOTH CALLERS. wsi_horizon_min_images_for_mode is the
queue's floor with the mode's own floor over it, and it is what the
capabilities query answers and what creation applies. The literal 3 and
the comment explaining it move there; the constant it becomes,
WSI_HORIZON_IMMEDIATE_MIN_IMAGES, sits beside WSI_HORIZON_MIN_IMAGES
and WSI_HORIZON_MAX_IMAGES where the other buffer counts are.

WHAT DOES NOT CHANGE. The extents do not depend on the present mode on
this backend, so the per-mode query answers the same currentExtent,
minImageExtent and maxImageExtent as the mode-agnostic one; and
maxImageCount is the design's fixed four either way. Only minImageCount
moves, and only when the caller asked about a mode — a query with
nothing chained still gets the queue's number, which is what the
specification means by the two being allowed to differ.

Nothing an application could previously do stops working: three images
is what an IMMEDIATE swapchain always got, and a minimum that is
published rather than applied silently is the same swapchain with the
number said out loud.
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c | 89 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 67 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c
index a272f5f..86ee8eb 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c
@@ -120,6 +120,12 @@
 #define WSI_HORIZON_MIN_IMAGES 2
 #define WSI_HORIZON_MAX_IMAGES 4
 
+/* And the floor IMMEDIATE has on top of that, which is a property of
+ * the compositor rather than of the queue: swapInterval 0 is honoured
+ * only with three or more buffers registered. See
+ * wsi_horizon_min_images_for_mode. */
+#define WSI_HORIZON_IMMEDIATE_MIN_IMAGES 3
+
 /* Smallest swapchain extent this backend offers, per side.
  *
  * MEASURED, not chosen: t_nwindow's extent ramp registered and presented
@@ -558,6 +564,50 @@ wsi_horizon_min_image_count(VkIcdSurfaceBase *surface)
    return MAX2(min_images, WSI_HORIZON_MIN_IMAGES);
 }
 
+/* THE FLOOR FOR ONE PRESENT MODE, which is not the same number for
+ * every mode — and that is why the capabilities query has to be told
+ * which mode is being asked about.
+ *
+ * IMMEDIATE TAKES THE THIRD IMAGE RATHER THAN QUIETLY BECOMING FIFO.
+ * swapInterval 0 is honoured by the compositor only with three or more
+ * buffers registered; below that the system enforces 1. The swap
+ * interval used to be computed as `image_count >= 3 ? 0 : 1` *after*
+ * the count was fixed, so an application asking for IMMEDIATE with two
+ * images — a count the published capabilities allow — got swapInterval
+ * 1 and a success code, which is FIFO wearing another mode's name.
+ * Advertising a present mode obliges implementing it for every valid
+ * swapchain. minImageCount is a minimum and the implementation chooses
+ * the actual count, so raising it is the conformant answer and needs no
+ * agreement from the application. Reported by Codex on PR #8.
+ *
+ * IT IS NOW PUBLISHED AND NOT ONLY APPLIED, which is the half that was
+ * missing. VK_KHR_surface_maintenance1 — advertised by this driver —
+ * lets an application ask for the capabilities of one present mode by
+ * chaining VkSurfacePresentModeKHR into
+ * vkGetPhysicalDeviceSurfaceCapabilities2KHR, and the specification
+ * says of that query that minImageCount and maxImageCount "are valid
+ * only for the specified presentMode". This backend answered the
+ * queue's mode-agnostic floor to every such question, so an application
+ * that asked about IMMEDIATE was told two and then given three behind
+ * its back: legal, because a minimum is a minimum, and useless, because
+ * the point of asking per mode is to find out what that mode costs.
+ * One function, both callers, and they cannot drift.
+ */
+static uint32_t
+wsi_horizon_min_images_for_mode(VkIcdSurfaceBase *surface,
+                                VkPresentModeKHR present_mode)
+{
+   uint32_t count = wsi_horizon_min_image_count(surface);
+
+   if (present_mode == VK_PRESENT_MODE_IMMEDIATE_KHR)
+      count = MAX2(count, WSI_HORIZON_IMMEDIATE_MIN_IMAGES);
+
+   /* A floor above the ceiling would be a capability nothing can
+    * satisfy: Vulkan requires maxImageCount to be at least
+    * minImageCount. */
+   return MIN2(count, WSI_HORIZON_MAX_IMAGES);
+}
+
 static VkResult
 wsi_horizon_surface_get_capabilities(VkIcdSurfaceBase *surface,
                                      struct wsi_device *wsi_device,
@@ -658,6 +708,16 @@ wsi_horizon_surface_get_capabilities2(VkIcdSurfaceBase *surface,
    if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
       return result;
 
+   /* ASKED ABOUT ONE MODE, ANSWERED ABOUT THAT MODE. The extents and
+    * the transforms do not depend on the present mode here; the image
+    * count does, and wsi_horizon_min_images_for_mode is the same
+    * function that will decide it at creation. */
+   if (present_mode != NULL) {
+      caps->surfaceCapabilities.minImageCount =
+         wsi_horizon_min_images_for_mode(surface,
+                                         present_mode->presentMode);
+   }
+
    vk_foreach_struct(ext, caps->pNext) {
       switch (ext->sType) {
       case VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_SURFACE_PROTECTED_CAPABILITIES_KHR: {
@@ -2949,29 +3009,14 @@ wsi_horizon_surface_create_swapchain(VkIcdSurfaceBase *icd_surface,
       wsi_swapchain_get_present_mode(wsi_device, pCreateInfo);
 
    uint32_t image_count = pCreateInfo->minImageCount;
-   /* The same floor the capabilities published, asked the same way, so a
-    * swapchain cannot end up below the minimum its own surface
-    * advertised. */
+   /* The same floor the capabilities published, asked the same way and
+    * about the same present mode, so a swapchain cannot end up below
+    * the minimum its own surface advertised — and an application that
+    * asked what IMMEDIATE costs cannot be surprised by the answer. See
+    * wsi_horizon_min_images_for_mode. */
    image_count = MAX2(image_count,
-                      wsi_horizon_min_image_count(icd_surface));
-
-   /* IMMEDIATE TAKES THE THIRD IMAGE RATHER THAN QUIETLY BECOMING FIFO.
-    *
-    * swapInterval 0 is honoured by the compositor only with three or
-    * more buffers registered; below that the system enforces 1. The
-    * swap interval used to be computed as `image_count >= 3 ? 0 : 1`
-    * *after* the count was fixed, so an application asking for
-    * IMMEDIATE with two images — a count the published capabilities
-    * allow — got swapInterval 1 and a success code, which is FIFO
-    * wearing another mode's name. Advertising a present mode obliges
-    * implementing it for every valid swapchain.
-    *
-    * minImageCount is a minimum and the implementation chooses the
-    * actual count, so raising it here is the conformant answer and
-    * needs no agreement from the application. Reported by Codex on
-    * PR #8. */
-   if (present_mode == VK_PRESENT_MODE_IMMEDIATE_KHR)
-      image_count = MAX2(image_count, 3);
+                      wsi_horizon_min_images_for_mode(icd_surface,
+                                                      present_mode));
    /* On the copy fallback the extra image buys nothing — libnx's
     * Framebuffer owns the window's slots and this count only sizes our
     * own staging images — but the path is not chosen yet here, and
-- 
